{"id": "EUVD-2026-76391", "enisaUuid": "2dedbe18-b802-3056-8c8c-a67c92442ad0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nlockd: pin next file across nlm_inspect_file lock-drop\n\nnlm_traverse_files() pins the current file with f_count++ across\na mutex_unlock for nlm_inspect_file(), but nothing pins the saved\nnext pointer.  A concurrent nlm_release_file() can kfree the next\nfile during the unlock window, and the iterator dereferences freed\nmemory on the next loop step.\n\nPin both current and next before the lock-drop.  Advance by\nswapping the pinned cursors at the end of each iteration so next\nis always held alive across the unlock.\n\nAlways call nlm_file_release() after dropping the iteration pin,\nregardless of whether the file matched the predicate.  Use\nnlm_file_inuse(), which does a live walk of the inode lock list,\nrather than the cached f_locks field, so skipped files that never\nran nlm_inspect_file() are evaluated correctly.\n\nBecause every file in a hash bucket is now pinned and released,\nfiles skipped by the is_failover_file predicate that have no\nlocks, blocks, shares, or external references are deleted during\ntraversal.  The old code never evaluated skipped files for\ncleanup.  The new behavior is intentional: such files are stale\nand should not persist in the table.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:43:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:47:35", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3c413f789eaf0170275c7eba523ead73d963f30", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/08a455f87b14c7ff22ae3fdadda62a796a3a5572", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/550c19222c7132c888e23c9d89079ba1c9bc4cca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/350087f231c11efcd288c310707c40eab63ca583", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c24bdb7df2f34bdc38ca8a73796f5acb40f1830c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/41f0a6d31615fcae261bf28a0aa50050dc93a401", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e999a88133654c6dfc68487fb49da5f20dfa2d4f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/526c49cff3f72c3ec74752016380c7567040581b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89485", "GHSA-wccq-x362-cg9j"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.71, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "34a342bf-4cdf-3d40-8bcd-f425a1eea858", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "3b41d1e5-9214-3c01-9bc7-d1617bca085d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "01df9c5e918ae5559f2d96da0143f8bfbb9e6171 <41f0a6d31615fcae261bf28a0aa50050dc93a401"}, {"id": "4a410738-c73f-38de-a4f2-0e928c33260b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "591cab69-2d85-31d2-8430-ce9ec28a12b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "5ad0a9e3-d279-3a53-9955-f97e84057f26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "01df9c5e918ae5559f2d96da0143f8bfbb9e6171 <08a455f87b14c7ff22ae3fdadda62a796a3a5572"}, {"id": "6a9dfd4e-496e-3c2f-be2c-8c540ffdc0e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "90bd1f76-469e-3814-a107-394df47d64e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "918740ae-26e5-3acc-9ab2-42c04bc6be0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "92cf7622-5253-3e58-a51e-06fa16345f10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "01df9c5e918ae5559f2d96da0143f8bfbb9e6171 <c24bdb7df2f34bdc38ca8a73796f5acb40f1830c"}, {"id": "93a44af4-b870-358e-9865-48e2ac031881", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "01df9c5e918ae5559f2d96da0143f8bfbb9e6171 <e3c413f789eaf0170275c7eba523ead73d963f30"}, {"id": "aae0bc6f-3b3d-395a-9f1b-266124c2fdfb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.18"}, {"id": "b2814496-fad2-3f12-8349-a5a7469ef0c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "01df9c5e918ae5559f2d96da0143f8bfbb9e6171 <e999a88133654c6dfc68487fb49da5f20dfa2d4f"}, {"id": "b9cf4706-c974-3c93-8fc3-dc3ea3a2904a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "ba0eb85a-fada-33ef-ad53-f4423d9eb5c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "01df9c5e918ae5559f2d96da0143f8bfbb9e6171 <550c19222c7132c888e23c9d89079ba1c9bc4cca"}, {"id": "c0a3382e-7847-3b88-9f08-e8566bf4dbfd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "01df9c5e918ae5559f2d96da0143f8bfbb9e6171 <526c49cff3f72c3ec74752016380c7567040581b"}, {"id": "c8c2b5b8-14b4-3016-a3f5-b54f386c87c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "01df9c5e918ae5559f2d96da0143f8bfbb9e6171 <350087f231c11efcd288c310707c40eab63ca583"}, {"id": "d439be22-2512-33e5-9ad2-5d14f4fc9a4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "eed2f97f-c729-379c-a67c-eb3af249313a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "938e4a9b-d714-341e-ae5c-8728c63086be", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}